      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>We should consider how ECM does this (if at all).  There was agreement at the london committer meeting<span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> to adopt ECM's extensibility approach. Not sure if that's relevant here.  If not, maybe an optional='true' attribute would make sense here.  Regardless of how it's done, a way to specify an optional datastream in a cmodel should be considered in scope for future releases of Fedora.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> <a href=\"http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCREPO/Feb+23-24+2010%2C+London+Committer+Meeting\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCREPO/Feb+23-24+2010%2C+London+Committer+Meeting</a></p>",
     "created": "20/Apr/10 12:50 PM",
